$create_video_index — build one FAISS HNSW index from all .ahvemb sidecars

SUMMARY
  For each videos[] file, looks for `.ahvemb/<video>.ahvemb` beside the source.
  Builds one shared FAISS HNSW index over all fragments from all videos, plus a
  mapping JSON file that points at the real video and .ahvemb paths on disk.
  Output bundle contains files[] only — one search index link.

SYNTAX
  $create_video_index

INPUT
  videos[] — source videos that already have `.ahvemb/<name>.ahvemb` sidecars

OUTPUT
  files[] only (all other arrays empty) — one link:
    videos.faiss       — normal mode (combined search index)
    videos.ahvmap.json — emulate mode only
  Sibling videos.ahvmap.json is always written on disk next to videos.faiss.

MAPPING FORMAT (.ahvmap.json)
  fragments — [{id, video, ahvemb, fps, start, end}, …] aligned with FAISS ids

BEHAVIOR
  Skips videos without `.ahvemb/<name>.ahvemb` or with empty sidecars.

DEPENDENCIES
  uv sync --extra video_index   (faiss-cpu, opencv-python, numpy)

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_CREATE_VIDEO_INDEX=1 — mapping JSON only (vectors embedded), no faiss.

EXAMPLE
  @all_videos: $folder('test_data', '*.mp4', source_path=True)
  @create_emb: @all_videos -> $add_video_embedding_files
  @index: @all_videos -> $create_video_index

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
